  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>An ice moon with a shallow brine ocean kept liquid by tidal flexing and leaking through a belt of parallel fractures, which is where the name comes from. It carries the only present-day heat source in the system that is not radiogenic. Mats recovered from the fractures are chemically distinct from anything on the neighbouring moons, and nobody can say why.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
  ],
